1749:{"seq":1749,"at":"2026-09-14T18:15:57.233Z","actor":"agent","type":"node.added","payload":{"id":"vi-sysdiag-grid-minimal","kind":"card","title":"From-scratch minimal-cell full grid: 12x22, down from 39x23","why":"Re-authored .werk/diagram-grid-full-minimal.wgrid from scratch instead of trimming diagram-grid-full-flat-narrow.wgrid further — the remaining width there was almost entirely caused by 2 long detour edges (gate_approvebar, cli_log) sprawling through columns other cards needed. Gave each detour its own dedicated column/jog instead, and every card defaults to 1x1 unless a real same-direction edge fan forces more.","status":"proto","who":"prototype"}}
1785:{"seq":1785,"at":"2026-09-14T20:18:29.542Z","actor":"agent","type":"note.added","payload":{"node":"vi-sysdiag-grid-mincell","text":"Followed through on the decision: removed the diagram-view switcher entirely (web/index.html + app.js) — Grid (full, minimal) is now the only diagram shown, no buttons to flip between prototypes. The old 'Debug' checkbox is now a small bug-icon button in the diagram's own top-right corner, toggling both the column-width overlay and the .wgrid source view below it together (one control, not two).\n\nAlso expanded diagram-grid-full-minimal.wgrid to include a 'diagram' card for itself, in MAP VIEW next to tree/graph3d/detail/rollup, with no edges (it reads .werk/diagram-*.svg straight off disk, not through GET /api/graph like its neighbours — wiring it to state would have been a false edge). Cost: 1 content line, 1 new column carried down every row. Placing it in the SAME row as its MAP VIEW siblings (not some other row) is what kept MAP VIEW's own frame from stretching into SERVER PROCESS's rows — directly the failure mode #vi-sysdiag-grid-groupshape wants a checker rule for, avoided here by hand. 0 build errors, 2586x1303 (was 2358x1303)."}}
1820:{"seq":1820,"at":"2026-09-14T21:11:52.244Z","actor":"agent","type":"note.added","payload":{"node":"vi-sysdiag-proto","text":"Two features landed on the Diagram view: #vi-sysdiag-zoomui (fit by default, 100% ceiling) and #vi-sysdiag-link (the card ids became a two-way link). #vi-sysdiag-link also puts real map card ids on all 23 nodes and all 22 edges of diagram-grid-full-minimal.wgrid — the fold #vi-sysdiag-derive claims an agent can do, now done and checkable by clicking."}}
1837:{"seq":1837,"at":"2026-09-14T22:08:19.913Z","actor":"agent","type":"note.added","payload":{"node":"vi-sysdiag-grid-lanewall","text":"Drawn for real in .werk/diagram-grid-full-minimal.wgrid. Two things did it: #vi-sysdiag-grid-junction's crossing (child->diagram + gate->approvebar share one cell, each blind to the other), and reordering runner's south fan so child sits next to the lane instead of on the far side of chatlog/lock — the actual blocker was never gate_approvebar alone, it was that child was positioned behind a cluster of uncrossable 1-hop bridge edges (runner->child, child->gate, child->cli), and junctions can't cross those (no pass-through cell). Moving child, not routing around it, is what worked. 0 build errors; verified programmatically that the resolved path actually starts at diagram and ends at child, and that all 22 prior cards/edges are still present. First attempt (a background agent trying to solve this by reasoning alone) failed by exhausting its output budget without acting — did it by hand instead, using the exact routing constraints already mapped out in conversation."}}
